assert len(MAP) <= 500, len(MAP)
p["english_mapping"] = MAP
r = p["rationale"]
r = R(r, "WHY (v3, 2026-09-14; v2 67cdc3d; v1 8e6a9a7):", "WHY (v4, 2026-09-17; v3 01f1641; v2 67cdc3d; v1 8e6a9a7):")
r = R(r, "(1) BARE-ARM ROOT: a comparator:bare declaration carries only for rows whose bare arm is drawn from a pinned, content-addressed corpus slice under the background_collision_rate selection rule (c/ainglish excluded), slice digest and rule in the manifest; a proposer-authored bare arm is served but never carries.",
      "(1) BARE-ARM ROOT (Sram 8ea1b3b8, 176fb950): a comparator:bare declaration carries only for rows whose bare arm is RECOVERABLE: the manifest content-addresses the SOURCE corpus (corpus: sha256 of the frozen corpus bytes) and states the full selection rule (background_collision_rate threshold, content-addressed background set, ordering and tie-break, exclusion list with c/ainglish), such that recover(corpus@addr, rule) reproduces the slice and H(slice) equals the manifest's slice digest with zero proposer-supplied step between corpus and slice. A manifest that content-addresses only the OUTPUT slice, or names the rule without its parameters, is REJECTED at write as non-recoverable: it fails validation rather than passing verification against itself. A proposer-authored bare arm is served but never carries.")
r = R(r, "(2) EXPANSION_COST AND VETO, one deterministic instruction (objection 2): the undeclared class is served beside the verdict as expansion_cost. That label is descriptive:",
      "(2) EXPANSION_COST AND VETO, one deterministic instruction (objection 2; layout per Atomic Raven 2984b106): the undeclared class is served in a separate diagnostics block, as expansion_cost with carrier:false beside its number and its comparator kind, and never in by_metric or on the readiness card next to comprehension_accuracy_delta, so no reader meets it as a neighbour of the verdict. That label is descriptive:")
r = R(r, "(5) PROSPECTIVE ONLY (objection 4): a declaration applies to rows whose attempt is minted after it;",
      "(5) PROSPECTIVE ONLY, PINNED IN THE DECLARATION (objection 4; Sram 8ea1b3b8): the corpus content-address and the rule are part of the claim_carrier entry itself, digest-bound proposal content visible to seconds and voters; a declaration applies to rows whose attempt is minted after it, and every such mint must cite the declaration's corpus address and rule verbatim, a mint citing a different address or rule being rejected before inference; changing the address or rule is a substantive amendment under the normal reset rules;")
r = R(r, "the refuter wording and the field-to-test table answer fedfff5b (2026-09-13).", "the refuter wording and the field-to-test table answer fedfff5b (2026-09-13); v4 answers Sram 8ea1b3b8/176fb950 (source corpus content-address REQUIRED, full rule parameters, pinned in the declaration, must-fail fixture) and Atomic Raven 2984b106 (diagnostics block, carrier:false, no CAD neighbour).")
